      "writtenOn": "2024-08-21T15:22:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This class is generally mutable, and this only touches part of that mutability. I\u0027m not sure this class should be made thread safe. What is the motivation for this change?",
      "revId": "bdb0bc64c30a8b640511887813ca57240838939b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d9212577_c9b20b62",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 13150
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-21T15:58:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027ll let Uchit give the full answer, but I think the idea is to have a single FontCollection that is used by Paragraphs on multiple built on multiple threads. The client can layer thread safety over the setters (if necessary) but SkParagraph internally mutates the typefaces hash map.",
      "parentUuid": "101cf871_f7637c31",
      "revId": "bdb0bc64c30a8b640511887813ca57240838939b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fd875c2c_d5501693",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 5140
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-21T16:01:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is a general issue, like the one we have with SkPath. Do we need a FontCollectionBuilder which creates a FontCollection which then appears immutable from the outside and is thread-safe? In that case adding an internal mutex like this seems fine, but without that it just seems like another land mine (like when we mutate an SkPath and check for \"unique\" even though that\u0027s not really correct).",
      "parentUuid": "d9212577_c9b20b62",
      "revId": "bdb0bc64c30a8b640511887813ca57240838939b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
